					<div style="text-align: center"><i><b><img src="https://i.postimg.cc/9FVm4X7v/24UMGIM39247-rgb.jpg" class="bbCodeImage LbImage" alt="[​IMG]" data-url="https://i.postimg.cc/9FVm4X7v/24UMGIM39247-rgb.jpg" style=""> </b></i>​</div><br>
<div style="text-align: center"><i><b>C,XOXO</b></i> is the fourth studio album by American singer <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Camila_Cabello" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Camila Cabello</a>. It was released on June 28, 2024, through <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geffen_Records" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Geffen</a> and <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Interscope_Records" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Interscope Records</a>, and is her first album following her departure from <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Epic_Records" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Epic Records</a>. Primarily a <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pop_music" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">pop</a> record, <i>C,XOXO</i> incorporates <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hyperpop" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">hyperpop</a>, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dance_music" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">dance</a>, and <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hip-hop_music" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">hip-hop</a> music. Guest vocalists include <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Playboi_Carti" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Playboi Carti</a>, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lil_Nas_X" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Lil Nas X</a>, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/JT_(rapper)" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">JT</a>, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yung_Miami" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Yung Miami</a>, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BLP_Kosher" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">BLP Kosher</a>, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Drake_(musician)" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Drake</a>, and uncredited vocals from <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PinkPantheress" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">PinkPantheress</a>, with the <i>Magic City Edition</i> including a collaboration with <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eem_Triplin" target="_blank" class="externalLink" rel="nofollow">Eem Triplin</a>.<br>
